  "functions": [
    "FUNC.XNPV"
  ],
  "kind": "quirk",
  "title": "XNPV rejects rate <= 0 with #NUM!, rejects non-numeric cells in vectors, and uses worksheet POWER",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0.20131 and 16.0.20527, XNPV(rate, values, dates) returns #NUM! for rate <= 0 (including rate = 0 and -0.0) while accepting +1e-300, rejects text, logicals, and blank cells inside values or dates with #VALUE!, rejects 2-D arrays with #REF!, truncates dates, and requires all dates >= dates[0]. It evaluates years = (date - anchor) / 365 in binary64, base = RN53(RN64(1 + rate)), pow = POWER(base, years), and x87 double-rounded division and sum.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured across 120 pinned XNPV rows in crates/calc-func/tests/witnesses/XNPV.json (Excel 16.0.20131) plus f3_financial (row 18) and prefix_metadata (row 395) in Excel 16.0.20527.20088, and matched across 3,406/3,406 full-bank and 120/120 pinned XNPV rows.",
